In 2018, just before Christmas, Terry lost her mom Durey. She was 72. A few days later, Terry went to the grocery store to pick up a few things. And I was, of course, feeling lots of emotions, but there was this numbness that prevailed over everything just so I could get through the day and take care of the tasks I needed to take care of. So I go to the checkout and the cashier greets me with how are you? And I just couldn't say fine or good and brush it off like that. I just felt I needed to say, you know what? I'm not doing great.

4
