My mother just passed away. And she responded expressed her sympathy and we finished up the transaction. So I turned to get my bag to leave and the young man who had bag my groceries looked me right in the eye and said, was it. Just a hug. But it wasn't just a hug. This man stood there and observed and listened and then reacted and gave the one thing that is most beautiful expression of comfort

